WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:06.702
A scalar subquery may return zero rows When that
happens PostgreSQL

00:00:06.728 --> 00:00:12.604
turns the missing scalar into NULL The requested
test ID in this example

00:00:12.630 --> 00:00:18.509
does not exist So the inner query returns no row and
the scalar

00:00:18.522 --> 00:00:24.097
result becomes NULL Remember this when the scalar
participates in a

00:00:24.124 --> 00:00:28.492
comparison because comparisons involving NULL follow
three-valued logic
